  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1...It will be another warm day today, with temperatures \ntrending lower into the weekend. \n\nAn upper level trough over eastern Canada will move south today, \ndisplacing a strong ridge over the eastern Great Lakes region. A \ncold front will move across the forecast area today, with cooler air \nfiltering in from north to south. This afternoon, 850mb temperatures \nwill fall into the mid teens across the eastern Lake Ontario region \nand the upper teens across western NY. Dewpoints will also be much \nlower during peak heating, resulting in more comfortable weather \ntoday. Another factor to the temperature forecast today is a west-\nnorthwest flow will allow smoke from Canadian wildfires to move into \nthe eastern Great Lakes today. Lowered maximum temperatures from NBM \nguidance today. A few showers are possible (~10%) across western NY \nthis afternoon, though most areas will remain dry. Smoke is expected \nto linger across the area through at least Thursday. \n\nAs the upper level trough deepens across the Great Lakes region, \ncooler temperatures aloft will move into the forecast area, \nresulting in a day to day cooling trend into the weekend.",
